Thermal Parameters Summary
* Preheat Zone: Temperature ramp rate of 1.5\text{ }^\circ\text{C/s} to 2.5\text{ }^\circ\text{C/s} up to 150\text{ }^\circ\text{C}. Evaporates volatile flux solvents gradually.
* Soak Zone: Maintain 150\text{ }^\circ\text{C} to 180\text{ }^\circ\text{C} for 60\text{ s} to 120\text{ s}. Equalizes thermal mass across multi-layer ground planes.
* Reflow Zone: Temperature held above liquidus (217\text{ }^\circ\text{C}) for 45\text{ s} to 75\text{ s}.
* Peak Temperature: 235\text{ }^\circ\text{C} to 245\text{ }^\circ\text{C} for 10\text{ s} to 20\text{ s} max. Exceeding 250\text{ }^\circ\text{C} risks interposer substrate damage.
* Cooling Zone: Ramp down rate at -2.0\text{ }^\circ\text{C/s} to -4.0\text{ }^\circ\text{C/s} to promote fine grain structure and maximum mechanical joint strength.
5.3 Micro-soldering Intervention Protocols
For Level 3 BGA rework, the system outputs explicit mechanical and chemical steps:
1. Underfill Clearance: Apply hot air at 160\text{ }^\circ\text{C} with a 3\text{ mm} curved nozzle. Gently scrape black epoxy underfill around the IC perimeter using a dental pick under 30\text{x} magnification.
2. BGA Extraction: Position PCB on bottom pre-heater set to 150\text{ }^\circ\text{C}. Apply top hot air at 350\text{ }^\circ\text{C} (airflow 60%) until solder liquefaction is achieved. Lift IC vertically with vacuum pickup pen.
3. Pad Preparation: Apply NC-559-ASM no-clean flux. Wick residual solder off PCB pads using leaded Sn63/Pb37 braid at 330\text{ }^\circ\text{C} iron tip temperature to flatten pads without lifting solder mask.
4. Reballing & Placement: Position direct-heat stencil over replacement IC. Apply SAC305 solder paste. Reflow at 240\text{ }^\circ\text{C}. Clean flux residue with 99.9\% Isopropyl Alcohol (IPA) before alignment and final board mounting.
6. Enterprise Boundaries, Compliance & Cloud Integration
To operate securely within commercial service environments, Triage AI Rev 4 implements compliance tracking, context handling rules, and seamless Point of Sale (POS) integrations.
6.1 Context Limits & Document Chunking Strategy
Motherboard schematics often consist of 100+ page PDF manuals and boardview netlists exceeding 50,000 nodes. Fitting this into LLM context windows requires specialized pre-chunking:
* Hierarchical Netlist Chunking: Rather than splitting text by arbitrary character counts, documents are parsed by schematic functional blocks (e.g., "System Agent Power Rail", "Thunderbolt 4 Retimer Interface", "DisplayPort Multiplexer").
* Overlap Strategy: Sub-chunks retain 15\% overlapping boundary nodes to ensure continuity of component connection paths across chunk edges.
* Context Compression: Vector retrievals extract top-k structural blocks, stripping decorative title blocks, page frames, and redundant legal disclaimers before injecting context into the prompt buffer.
6.2 NIST SP 800-88 Rev 1 Data Sanitization Audit Trails
When triage involves servicing storage devices (NVMe drives, onboard NAND flash), Triage AI Rev 4 tracks data destruction compliance:
* Sanitization Methods: Supports Cryptographic Erasure (CE) and ATA/NVMe Block Erase commands.
* Verification Hash: Once sanitization completes, the system computes a SHA-256 digital signature incorporating device serial number, technician ID, erasure method, and timestamp.
* Audit Trail Storage: Certificates are saved as immutable JSON records in Vercel Postgres, downloadable as formatted PDF audit compliance reports.
